# Go code quality

Cursor must not run Docker or `./scripts/check-quality.sh` (pinned images and
module tags live in that script).

After changing Go files, run locally in the touched modules (offline only):

- `gofmt -l` on changed files (or `gofmt -w` to fix)
- `./scripts/offline-go.sh vet ./...`
- `./scripts/offline-go.sh test ./...` (add `-tags …` from that module's `.quality-tags` when the file exists)

All local Go commands use `./scripts/offline-go.sh` (`GOPROXY=off`, `-mod=readonly`). Never
`go install` or `go run` with a remote module version (`go run …@…`). If the module cache misses,
stop — do not download modules to fix it. Rerun the full suite after any edit, including placeholder scrubs.

In your report, list the changed Go files and ask Francis to run
`./scripts/check-quality.sh --fast`, and the full script before a release.

Prefer real fixes over `//nolint`. If a nolint is truly needed, scope it to the specific linter and add a reason comment.

Do not edit `.golangci.yml` or `scripts/check-quality.sh` to silence issues unless the user asks.
